# v2 bulk BCC Li reference energy with the same SNAP potential
# Build the reference cell first:
#   python -m generator.bulk --outdir ../outputs/bulk
# Usage:
#   lmp -in in.bulk_energy -var outdir ../outputs \
#       -var kim_model SNAP_ZuoChenLi_2019_Li__MO_732106099012_000
units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p
read_data ${outdir}/bulk/bulk_Li.data
read_data outputs/bulk/bulk_Li.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (14.04 14.04 14.04)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  128 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  128 velocities
  read_data CPU = 0.001 seconds
pair_style kim ${kim_model}
pair_style kim SNAP_ZuoChenLi_2019_Li__MO_732106099012_000
pair_coeff * * Li
neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes
# bulk: all three directions are true lattice directions -> relax all at P=0
fix 1 all box/relax iso 0.0
min_style cg
thermo 100
thermo_style custom step pe etotal press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
minimize 0.0 1.0e-6 10000 100000

